<h3>CHAPTER 2: Windowing Dynamics, Leveling & Display Optimization</h3>

<p>Because the human eye can only perceive around 20 to 30 shades of grey, CT image viewing depends on adjusting <strong>Window Width (WW)</strong> and <strong>Window Level (WL)</strong> to accentuate specific tissue density ranges.</p>

<h4>2.1 Mathematical Basis of Windowing</h4>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Window Width (WW):</strong> Controls image contrast range. A wide window displays a broad range of densities (low contrast), whereas a narrow window increases image contrast.</li>
  <li><strong>Window Level (WL):</strong> Controls image brightness by centering the window display around the average Hounsfield Unit of the target anatomy.</li>
  <li><em>Upper Display Limit = WL + (WW / 2)</em></li>
  <li><em>Lower Display Limit = WL - (WW / 2)</em></li>
</ul>

<h4>2.2 Standard Diagnostic Window Settings</h4>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Anatomical Region / Target</th>
      <th>Window Width (WW)</th>
      <th>Window Level (WL)</th>
      <th>Diagnostic Objective</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Brain Soft Tissue</strong></td>
      <td>80 HU</td>
      <td>+40 HU</td>
      <td>Differentiates grey/white matter junction and subtle ischemic changes.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Subdural / Epidural Window</strong></td>
      <td>130 to 200 HU</td>
      <td>+50 to +70 HU</td>
      <td>Distinguishes hyperdense extra-axial blood from adjacent skull bone.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Lung Parenchyma</strong></td>
      <td>1500 HU</td>
      <td>-600 HU</td>
      <td>Evaluates pulmonary nodules, interstitial markings, and air bronchograms.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Mediastinum / Soft Tissue</strong></td>
      <td>350 to 400 HU</td>
      <td>+40 to +50 HU</td>
      <td>Inspects vascular structures, lymph nodes, and cardiac borders.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Abdomen / Pelvis</strong></td>
      <td>350 to 400 HU</td>
      <td>+40 to +50 HU</td>
      <td>Delineates solid organs, mesenteric fat stranding, and fluid.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Bone Window</strong></td>
      <td>2000 to 2500 HU</td>
      <td>+500 HU</td>
      <td>Inspects cortical bone fractures, trabecular destruction, and sinus walls.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

