  <strong>AI Prompt:</strong> <code>3D medical diagram illustrating acute CT head trauma patterns: biconvex Epidural Hematoma, crescentic Subdural Hematoma, and hyperdense Subarachnoid Hemorrhage in basal cisterns, dark navy backdrop with glowing cyan callouts, 8k --ar 16:9</code>
</div>

<br/>

<h3>CHAPTER 5: Artifacts, Radiation Dose Optimization & Pre-Flight Checklists</h3>

<h4>5.1 Common CT Artifacts & Mitigation Strategies</h4>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Metal Streak Artifact:</strong> High atomic number metallic objects cause beam hardening and photon starvation streaks. <em>Mitigation:</em> Utilize iterative reconstruction algorithms (e.g., MAR/iMAR) and tilt gantry to avoid direct metal plane.</li>
  <li><strong>Beam Hardening Artifact:</strong> Polychromatic X-ray beam becomes harder (higher average energy) as lower energy photons are absorbed, producing broad dark bands between dense bones (e.g., posterior fossa).</li>
  <li><strong>Motion Artifact:</strong> Patient movement during acquisition produces shading and ghosting streaks. <em>Mitigation:</em> Shorten rotation time, utilize prospective gating, and implement fixation devices.</li>
</ul>

<h4>5.2 Dose Optimization Principles (ALARA & Dose Metrics)</h4>
<ul>
  <li><strong>CTDIvol (Volume CT Dose Index):</strong> Measures average radiation dose delivered to a standardized phantom within the scan volume (mGy).</li>
  <li><strong>DLP (Dose Length Product):</strong> Measures total radiation exposure by integrating CTDIvol over total scan length (mGy·cm). <em>Effective Dose (mSv) = DLP &times; Conversion Factor (k)</em>.</li>
  <li><strong>Automatic Exposure Control (AEC / Tube Current Modulation):</strong> Dynamically adjusts mA based on patient thickness along the z-axis to maintain uniform image noise while minimizing patient dose.</li>
</ul>

<h4>5.3 CT Technologist Pre-Scan Verification Checklist</h4>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Verification Step</th>
      <th>Standard Operating Parameter</th>
      <th>Status</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Patient Verification & Lab Status</td>
      <td>Two patient identifiers, serum Creatinine / eGFR check (&gt;30 mL/min)</td>
      <td>[  ] Pass</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Allergy & Contrast History</td>
      <td>Rule out prior anaphylactoid reaction to iodinated contrast media</td>
      <td>[  ] Pass</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>IV Cannula Patency</td>
      <td>18G to 20G peripheral IV access checked with saline flush for power injection</td>
      <td>[  ] Pass</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Scan Range & Positioning</td>
      <td>Laser alignment at anatomical landmark; clear metal objects from scan field</td>
      <td>[  ] Pass</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Protocol Selection</td>
      <td>Adjust kVp/mA based on weight/age; verify automatic bolus tracking ROI</td>
      <td>[  ] Pass</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Post-Scan Dose Review</td>
      <td>Review CTDIvol and DLP metrics against diagnostic reference levels (DRLs)</td>
      <td>[  ] Pass</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

